            whatItAsks: "Test $H_0: \\beta_j = 0$ (or $\\beta_j = c$) at significance level $\\alpha$ - **Appeared in**: [[Cleaned Past Questions/2025 Q1]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2024 Q5]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2023 Q3]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2022 Q1]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2021 Q3]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2020 Q3]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2019 Q1]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2018 Q1]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2017 Q1]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2016 Q7]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2015 Q1]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2014 Q6]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/WS1 Q14]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/WS1 Q15]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/WS4 Q2]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/WS4 Q3]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/WS4 Q4]] - **Relevant concepts**: [[Concepts/Hypothesis Testing]], [[Concepts/p-values]]",
            steps: ["State the hypotheses: **Two-sided**: $H_0: \\beta_j = c$ vs $H_1: \\beta_j \\neq c$ | **One-sided**: $H_0: \\beta_j = c$ vs $H_1: \\beta_j > c$ (or $H_1: \\beta_j < c$) 2. Compute the t-statistic: $$t^{\\text{act}} = \\frac{\\hat{\\beta}_j - c}{\\text{se}(\\hat{\\beta}_j)}$$ 3. State the null distribution: Under $H_0$, $t^{\\text{act}} \\xrightarrow{d} N(0,1)$ 4. For two-sided at 5%: Critical value $1.96$, reject if $|t^{\\text{act}}| > 1.96$ 5. For one-sided at 5%: Critical value $1.645$, reject if $t^{\\text{act}} > 1.645$ 6. Compute p-value: Two-sided: $p = 2[1 - \\Phi(|t^{\\text{act}}|)]$ 7. Conclude: Reject $H_0$ if $p < \\alpha$ 8. Common mistakes: Saying 'accept' instead of 'fail to reject', misinterpreting p-value, wrong critical values"],
