            steps: ["Identify the test statistic and null distribution 2. For two-sided ($H_1: \\beta_j \\neq c$): $p = 2[1 - \\Phi(|t^{\\text{act}}|)]$ 3. For one-sided upper ($H_1: \\beta_j > c$): $p = 1 - \\Phi(t^{\\text{act}})$ 4. For one-sided lower ($H_1: \\beta_j < c$): $p = \\Phi(t^{\\text{act}})$ 5. Use standard normal tables to compute $p$ 6. Interpretation: $p$ is probability of observing test statistic as extreme if $H_0$ true 7. Decision: Reject $H_0$ at level $\\alpha$ if $p < \\alpha$ 8. Common mistakes: Saying p-value is probability $H_0$ is true, halving without checking direction"],
