            steps: ["Start with fitted model: $\\widehat{Y} = \\hat{\\beta}_0 + \\hat{\\beta}_1 X + \\hat{\\beta}_2 X^2$ 2. Marginal effect: $\\frac{\\partial \\widehat{Y}}{\\partial X} = \\hat{\\beta}_1 + 2\\hat{\\beta}_2 X$ (depends on level of $X$) 3. At sample mean: ME $|_{X=\\bar{X}} = \\hat{\\beta}_1 + 2\\hat{\\beta}_2\\bar{X}$ 4. At policy value: ME $|_{X=X_0} = \\hat{\\beta}_1 + 2\\hat{\\beta}_2 X_0$ 5. Standard error via delta method: $\\text{se}(\\text{ME}) = \\sqrt{\\text{Var}(\\hat{\\beta}_1) + (2X)^2 \\text{Var}(\\hat{\\beta}_2) + 2(2X)\\text{Cov}(\\hat{\\beta}_1, \\hat{\\beta}_2)}$ 6. Confidence interval: ME $\\pm 1.96 \\cdot$ se(ME) 7. Hypothesis test: $t = $ ME / se(ME), reject if $|t| > 1.96$ 8. Interaction: If $Y = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 X + \\beta_2 X \\cdot Z + u$, then $\\partial Y/\\partial X = \\beta_1 + \\beta_2 Z$ 9. Common mistakes: Using only $\\hat{\\beta}_1$, computing at wrong $X$ value, confusing marginal effect with elasticity"],
