            steps: ["Fit nonlinear model: $Y_i = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 X_i + \\beta_2 X_i^2 + u_i$ 2. Hypotheses: $H_0: \\beta_2 = 0$ (linear) vs $H_1: \\beta_2 \\neq 0$ (nonlinear) 3. t-statistic: $t^{\\text{act}} = \\hat{\\beta}_2 / \\text{se}(\\hat{\\beta}_2)$ 4. Critical value: Two-sided 5%, reject if $|t| > 1.96$ 5. p-value: $p = 2[1 - \\Phi(|t|)]$ 6. If $p < 0.05$: Quadratic term significant, relationship is nonlinear 7. F-test alternative: Compare linear SSR$_L$ vs quadratic SSR$_Q$: $F = [(SSR_L - SSR_Q)/1] / [SSR_Q/(n-3)]$ 8. Common mistake: Confusing statistical significance with practical significance (significant term may have negligible effect)"],
