            steps: ["Heteroskedasticity affects inference through standard errors 2. Homoskedastic SEs wrong under heteroskedasticity 3. Robust SEs correct under both homoskedasticity and heteroskedasticity 4. Testing: Use robust SEs for hypothesis tests 5. Confidence intervals: Use robust SEs for correct coverage 6. Best practice: Always report robust SEs in applied work 7. Trade-off: Robust SEs slightly larger under homoskedasticity but conservative 8. Software: Most packages offer 'robust' or 'HC' SE options (HC0, HC1, HC2, HC3)"],
