            name: "State IV conditions (relevance, exogeneity, exclusion)",
            whatItAsks: "What conditions must an instrument Z satisfy? - **Step-by-step guide**: 1. Define the structural model: $Y = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 X + u$ where $\\text{Cov}(X, u) \\neq 0$ (endogenous) ([[Concepts/Instrumental Variables]]) 2. State the **first IV condition — Relevance (Z1)**: $\\text{Cov}(Z, X) \\neq 0$ (or $\\text{Corr}(Z, X) \\neq 0$) - Interpretation: the instrument must be correlated with the endogenous regressor - If Z is uncorrelated with X, it provides no information about the endogenous variation in X - Test: First-stage F-statistic $> 10$ indicates strong relevance ([[Concepts/Weak Instruments]]) 3. State the **second IV condition — Exogeneity (Z2)**: $\\text{Cov}(Z, u) = 0$ (or $E[u|Z] = 0$) - Interpretation: the instrument is uncorrelated with the structural error - Z must not directly affect Y except through X; confounders of both Z and Y violate this - **Cannot be tested** with a single instrument; requires institutional/economic reasoning ([[Concepts/Instrument Validity and Testing]]) 4. State the **third IV condition — Exclusion Restriction**: Z does not appear as a regressor in the structural equation - Mathematically: the true model is $Y = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 X + u$ (not $Y = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 X + \\beta_2 Z + u$) - If Z directly affects Y, it cannot serve as a valid instrument (violates both exclusion and exogeneity) 5. Summarize the **validity conditions**: - Z1 (Relevance): $\\text{Cov}(Z, X) \\neq 0$ — empirically testable - Z2 (Exogeneity): $\\text{Cov}(Z, u) = 0$ — requires economic/institutional argument - Z3 (Exclusion): Z appears only indirectly through X 6. Note: with multiple instruments, the conditions must hold **jointly**; weak relevance in any instrument undermines the entire estimator ([[Concepts/Instrumental Variables]]) - **Appeared in**: [[Cleaned Past Questions/2020 Q5]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2020 Q7]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2021 Q5]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2022 Q4]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2022 Q5]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2023 Q5]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2023 Q6]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2024 Q4]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2024 Q6]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2025 Q4]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/2025 Q6]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/WS6 Q1]], [[Cleaned Past Questions/WS6 Q2]] - **Relevant concepts**: [[Concepts/Instrumental Variables]], [[Concepts/Instrument Validity and Testing]]",
